  "technical_issues": [
    {
      "where": "Project Plan & Preliminary Progress",
      "issue": "A 600 km orbit is low Earth orbit, not geostationary. Geostationary altitude is approximately 35,786 km above the equator; moreover, a geostationary satellite cannot remain directly overhead of the Great Barrier Reef, which is south of the equator."
    },
    {
      "where": "Mission Concept & Rationale",
      "issue": "The stated 2016 and 2017 coral-loss percentages appear to conflate bleaching extent with coral mortality and are presented as whole-reef losses without qualification. Verify the figures and distinguish bleaching from mortality and local from reef-wide estimates."
    }
  ],
  "overall": "The report communicates a relevant Australian mission need, identifies users, and provides a useful initial work plan. Its main weakness is the lack of preliminary engineering results, compounded by a fundamental error in the proposed orbit. Clarifying mission performance needs, correcting the orbit, and adding initial calculations or STK outputs would substantially strengthen the submission."
}
